nv-define-space2-external-nv: TPM2_NV_DefineSpace2 rejects external NV Indexes it cannot support

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 2, Table "Definition of TPMT_NV_PUBLIC_2
Structure": "The handleType member is the same as the first byte of the public
member, the nvIndex field."; Part 2, Table "Definition of
TPMS_NV_PUBLIC_EXP_ATTR Structure": "nvIndex | TPMI_RH_NV_EXP_INDEX | the
handle of the data area"; Part 3, TPM2_NV_DefineSpace2: "allowing all types of
NV indices that support DefineSpace to be defined").

For handleType = TPM_HT_EXTERNAL_NV, NvPublicFromNvPublic2() copies the
attributes, authPolicy, dataSize and nameAlg of the TPMS_NV_PUBLIC_EXP_ATTR
but not its nvIndex, so NvDefineSpace() checks and defines an Index whose
handle is uninitialized stack memory (undefined behavior; the Index the caller
named is not created). The reference cannot use external NV Indexes anyway:
EntityGetLoadStatus() rejects every TPM_HT_EXTERNAL_NV handle ("Not yet
supported", TPM_RC_VALUE), so such an Index could neither be read, written nor
undefined. The external NV case is compiled out, so TPM2_NV_DefineSpace2
rejects the handle type like any other one it does not support
(TPM_RC_HANDLE + publicInfo, its default case), as tpm-rs, which does not
implement external NV Indexes, does.
diff --git a/src/NVCommands.c b/src/NVCommands.c
--- a/src/NVCommands.c
+++ b/src/NVCommands.c
@@ -890,7 +890,12 @@ TPM2_NV_DefineSpace2(NV_DefineSpace2_In* in  // IN: input parameter list
 	{
 	  case TPM_HT_NV_INDEX:
 	    break;
-#  if EXTERNAL_NV
+#  if EXTERNAL_NV && 0  // tpm-rs differential testing -- spec deviation fix (NOT
+                        // determinism): an external NV Index is defined with an
+                        // uninitialized nvIndex (NvPublicFromNvPublic2() does not
+                        // copy it) and could never be loaded (EntityGetLoadStatus:
+                        // "Not yet supported", TPM_RC_VALUE), so reject the handle
+                        // type like the other unsupported ones (default case).
 	  case TPM_HT_EXTERNAL_NV:
 	    // The reference implementation may let you define an "external" NV
 	    // index, but it doesn't currently support setting any of the extended
